    "text": "Brocen wurde.\nHet \u00fea hyssa hw\u00e6ne hors forl\u00e6tan, feor afysan, and for\u00f0 gangan, hicgan to handum and to hige godum.\n\u00dea \u00fe\u00e6t Offan m\u00e6g \u00e6rest onfunde, \u00fe\u00e6t se eorl nolde yrh\u00f0o ge\u00feolian, he let him \u00fea of handon leofne\nBe \u00feam man mihte oncnawan \u00fe\u00e6t se cniht nolde wacian \u00e6t \u00feam wige, \u00fea he to w\u00e6pnum feng.\nEac him wolde Eadric his ealdre gel\u00e6stan, frean to gefeohte, ongan \u00fea for\u00f0 beran gar to gu\u00fee.\nHe h\u00e6fde god ge\u00feanc \u00fea hwile \u00fee he mid handum healdan mihte bord and bradswurd.\nBeot he gel\u00e6ste \u00fea he \u00e6tforan his frean feohtan sceolde.\n\u00d0a \u00fe\u00e6r Byrhtno\u00f0 ongan beornas trymian, rad and r\u00e6dde, rincum t\u00e6hte hu hi sceoldon standan and \u00feone\nAnd b\u00e6d \u00fe\u00e6t hyra randas rihte heoldon f\u00e6ste mid folman, and ne forhtedon na.\n\u00dea he h\u00e6fde \u00fe\u00e6t folc f\u00e6gere getrymmed, he lihte \u00fea mid leodon \u00fe\u00e6r him leofost w\u00e6s, \u00fe\u00e6r he his\n\u00dea stod on st\u00e6\u00f0e, sti\u00f0lice clypode wicinga ar, wordum m\u00e6lde, se on beot abead brimli\u00feendra \u00e6r\u00e6nde to\nMe sendon to \u00fee s\u00e6men snelle, heton \u00f0e secgan \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu most sendan ra\u00f0e beagas wi\u00f0 gebeorge; and\nNe \u00feurfe we us spillan, gif ge speda\u00fe to \u00feam; we willa\u00f0 wi\u00f0 \u00feam golde gri\u00f0 f\u00e6stnian.\nGyf \u00feu \u00feat ger\u00e6dest, \u00fee her ricost eart, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu \u00feine leoda lysan wille, syllan s\u00e6mannum on hyra sylfra\nByrhtno\u00f0 ma\u00feelode, bord hafenode, wand wacne \u00e6sc, wordum m\u00e6lde, yrre and anr\u00e6d ageaf him\nHi willa\u00f0 eow to gafole garas syllan, \u00e6ttrynne ord and ealde swurd, \u00fea heregeatu \u00fee eow \u00e6t hilde ne\nBrimmanna boda, abeod eft ongean, sege \u00feinum leodum miccle la\u00fere spell, \u00fe\u00e6t her stynt unforcu\u00f0 eorl\nFeallan sceolon h\u00e6\u00feene \u00e6t hilde.\nTo heanlic me \u00feince\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t ge mid urum sceattum to scype gangon unbefohtene, nu ge \u00feus feor hider on\nNe sceole ge swa softe sinc gegangan; us sceal ord and ecg \u00e6r geseman, grim gu\u00f0plega, \u00e6r we gofol\nHet \u00fea bord beran, beornas gangan, \u00fe\u00e6t hi on \u00feam easte\u00f0e ealle stodon.\nNe mihte \u00fe\u00e6r for w\u00e6tere werod to \u00feam o\u00f0rum; \u00fe\u00e6r com flowende flod \u00e6fter ebban, lucon\nTo lang hit him \u00feuhte, hw\u00e6nne hi tog\u00e6dere garas beron.\nHi \u00fe\u00e6r Pantan stream mid prasse bestodon, Eastseaxena ord and se \u00e6schere.\nNe mihte hyra \u00e6nig o\u00ferum derian, buton hwa \u00feurh flanes flyht fyl gename.\nSe flod ut gewat; \u00fea flotan stodon gearowe, wicinga fela, wiges georne.\nHet \u00fea h\u00e6le\u00f0a hleo healdan \u00fea bricge wigan wigheardne, se w\u00e6s haten Wulfstan, cafne mid his cynne,\n\u00de\u00e6r stodon mid Wulfstane wigan unforhte, \u00c6lfere and Maccus, modige twegen, \u00fea noldon \u00e6t \u00feam\n\u00dea hi \u00fe\u00e6t ongeaton and georne gesawon \u00fe\u00e6t hi \u00fe\u00e6r bricgweardas bitere fundon, ongunnon lytegian \u00fea\n\u00d0a se eorl ongan for his ofermode alyfan landes to fela la\u00feere \u00f0eode.\nOngan ceallian \u00fea ofer cald w\u00e6ter Byrhtelmes bearn beornas gehlyston: Nu eow is gerymed, ga\u00f0 ricene\nWodon \u00fea w\u00e6lwulfas for w\u00e6tere ne murnon, wicinga werod, west ofer Pantan, ofer scir w\u00e6ter scyldas\n\u00de\u00e6r ongean gramum gearowe stodon Byrhtno\u00f0 mid beornum; he mid bordum het wyrcan \u00feone\n\u00dea w\u00e6s feohte neh, tir \u00e6t getohte.\nW\u00e6s seo tid cumen \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r f\u00e6ge men feallan sceoldon.\n\u00de\u00e6r wear\u00f0 hream ahafen, hremmas wundon, earn \u00e6ses georn; w\u00e6s on eor\u00fean cyrm.\nHi leton \u00fea of folman feolhearde speru, gegrundene garas fleogan; bogan w\u00e6ron bysige, bord ord\nBiter w\u00e6s se beadur\u00e6s, beornas feollon on gehw\u00e6\u00f0ere hand, hyssas lagon.\nWund wear\u00f0 Wulfm\u00e6r, w\u00e6lr\u00e6ste geceas, Byrhtno\u00f0es m\u00e6g; he mid billum wear\u00f0, his swuster sunu,\n\u00de\u00e6r wear\u00f0 wicingum wi\u00feerlean agyfen.\nGehyrde ic \u00fe\u00e6t Eadweard anne sloge swi\u00f0e mid his swurde, swenges ne wyrnde \u00fe\u00e6t him \u00e6t fotum\nSwa stemnetton sti\u00f0hicgende hysas \u00e6t hilde, hogodon georne hwa \u00fe\u00e6r mid orde \u00e6rost mihte on\nStodon st\u00e6def\u00e6ste; stihte hi Byrhtno\u00f0, b\u00e6d \u00fe\u00e6t hyssa gehwylc hogode to wige \u00fee on Denon wolde\nWod \u00fea wiges heard, w\u00e6pen up ahof, bord to gebeorge, and wi\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6s beornes stop.\nEode swa anr\u00e6d eorl to \u00feam ceorle, \u00e6g\u00feer hyra o\u00f0rum yfeles hogode.\nSende \u00f0a se s\u00e6rinc su\u00feerne gar, \u00fe\u00e6t gewundod wear\u00f0 wigena hlaford; he sceaf \u00fea mid \u00f0am scylde,\nGegremod wear\u00f0 se gu\u00f0rinc; he mid gare stang wlancne wicing, \u00fee him \u00fea wunde forgeaf.\nFrod w\u00e6s se fyrdrinc; he let his francan wadan \u00feurh \u00f0\u00e6s hysses hals, hand wisode \u00fe\u00e6t he on \u00feam\n\u00d0a he o\u00feerne ofstlice sceat, \u00fe\u00e6t seo byrne tob\u00e6rst; he w\u00e6s on breostum wund \u00feurh \u00f0a hringlocan, him\nSe eorl w\u00e6s \u00fee bli\u00fera, hloh \u00fea, modi man, s\u00e6de metode \u00feanc \u00f0\u00e6s d\u00e6gweorces \u00fee him drihten forgeaf.\nForlet \u00fea drenga sum daro\u00f0 of handa, fleogan of folman, \u00fe\u00e6t se to for\u00f0 gewat \u00feurh \u00f0one \u00e6\u00feelan\nHim be healfe stod hyse unweaxen, cniht on gecampe, se full caflice br\u00e6d of \u00feam beorne blodigne\nOrd in gewod, \u00fe\u00e6t se on eor\u00fean l\u00e6g \u00fee his \u00feeoden \u00e6r \u00feearle ger\u00e6hte.\nEode \u00fea gesyrwed secg to \u00feam eorle; he wolde \u00fe\u00e6s beornes beagas gefecgan, reaf and hringas and\n\u00dea Byrhtno\u00f0 br\u00e6d bill of sce\u00f0e, brad and bruneccg, and on \u00fea byrnan sloh.\nTo ra\u00fee hine gelette lidmanna sum, \u00fea he \u00fe\u00e6s eorles earm amyrde.\nFeoll \u00fea to foldan fealohilte swurd; ne mihte he gehealdan heardne mece, w\u00e6pnes wealdan.\n\u00dea gyt \u00fe\u00e6t word gecw\u00e6\u00f0 har hilderinc, hyssas bylde, b\u00e6d gangan for\u00f0 gode geferan; ne mihte \u00fea on\nHe to heofenum wlat: Ge\u00feancie \u00fee, \u00f0eoda waldend, ealra \u00fe\u00e6ra wynna \u00fee ic on worulde gebad.\nNu ic ah, milde metod, m\u00e6ste \u00feearfe \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu minum gaste godes geunne, \u00fe\u00e6t min sawul to \u00f0e si\u00f0ian\nIc eom frymdi to \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t hi helscea\u00f0an hynan ne moton.\n\u00d0a hine heowon h\u00e6\u00f0ene scealcas and begen \u00fea beornas \u00fee him big stodon, \u00c6lfno\u00f0 and Wulm\u00e6r\nHi bugon \u00fea fram beaduwe \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6r beon noldon.\n\u00de\u00e6r wear\u00f0 Oddan bearn \u00e6rest on fleame, Godric fram gu\u00fee, and \u00feone godan forlet \u00fee him m\u00e6nigne\nHe gehleop \u00feone eoh \u00fee ahte his hlaford, on \u00feam ger\u00e6dum \u00fee hit riht ne w\u00e6s, and his bro\u00f0ru mid him\nAc wendon fram \u00feam wige and \u00feone wudu sohton, flugon on \u00fe\u00e6t f\u00e6sten and hyra feore burgon, and\nSwa him Offa on d\u00e6g \u00e6r as\u00e6de on \u00feam me\u00feelstede, \u00fea he gemot h\u00e6fde, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r modiglice manega\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 afeallen \u00fe\u00e6s folces ealdor, \u00c6\u00feelredes eorl; ealle gesawon heor\u00f0geneatas \u00fe\u00e6t hyra heorra\n\u00dea \u00f0\u00e6r wendon for\u00f0 wlance \u00feegenas, unearge men efston georne; hi woldon \u00fea ealle o\u00f0er twega, lif\nSwa hi bylde for\u00f0 bearn \u00c6lfrices, wiga wintrum geong, wordum m\u00e6lde, \u00c6lfwine \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0, he on\nGemunan \u00fea m\u00e6la \u00fee we oft \u00e6t meodo spr\u00e6con, \u00feonne we on bence beot ahofon, h\u00e6le\u00f0 on healle,\nIc wylle mine \u00e6\u00feelo eallum gecy\u00fean, \u00fe\u00e6t ic w\u00e6s on Myrcon miccles cynnes; w\u00e6s min ealda f\u00e6der\nNe sceolon me on \u00fe\u00e6re \u00feeode \u00feegenas \u00e6twitan \u00fe\u00e6t ic of \u00f0isse fyrde feran wille, eard gesecan, nu min\nMe is \u00fe\u00e6t hearma m\u00e6st; he w\u00e6s \u00e6g\u00f0er min m\u00e6g and min hlaford.\n\u00dea he for\u00f0 eode, f\u00e6h\u00f0e gemunde, \u00fe\u00e6t he mid orde anne ger\u00e6hte flotan on \u00feam folce, \u00fe\u00e6t se on foldan\nOngan \u00fea winas manian, frynd and geferan, \u00fe\u00e6t hi for\u00f0 eodon.\nOffa gem\u00e6lde, \u00e6scholt asceoc: Hw\u00e6t \u00feu, \u00c6lfwine, hafast ealle gemanode \u00feegenas to \u00feearfe, nu ure\nUs is eallum \u00feearf \u00fe\u00e6t ure \u00e6ghwylc o\u00feerne bylde wigan to wige, \u00fea hwile \u00fee he w\u00e6pen m\u00e6ge habban\nUs Godric h\u00e6f\u00f0, earh Oddan bearn, ealle beswicene.\nWende \u00fe\u00e6s formoni man, \u00fea he on meare rad, on wlancan \u00feam wicge, \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6re hit ure hlaford;\nAbreo\u00f0e his angin, \u00fe\u00e6t he her swa manigne man aflymde.\nLeofsunu gem\u00e6lde and his linde ahof, bord to gebeorge; he \u00feam beorne oncw\u00e6\u00f0: Ic \u00fe\u00e6t gehate, \u00fe\u00e6t ic\nNe \u00feurfon me embe Sturmere stedef\u00e6ste h\u00e6l\u00e6\u00f0 wordum \u00e6twitan, nu min wine gecranc, \u00fe\u00e6t ic\nHe ful yrre wod, feaht f\u00e6stlice, fleam he forhogode.\nDunnere \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0, daro\u00f0 acwehte, unorne ceorl, ofer eall clypode, b\u00e6d \u00fe\u00e6t beorna gehwylc Byrhtno\u00f0\n\u00dea hi for\u00f0 eodon, feores hi ne rohton; ongunnon \u00fea hiredmen heardlice feohtan, grame garberend, and\nHim se gysel ongan geornlice fylstan; he w\u00e6s on Nor\u00f0hymbron heardes cynnes, Ecglafes bearn, him\nHe ne wandode na \u00e6t \u00feam wigplegan, ac he fysde for\u00f0 flan genehe; hwilon he on bord sceat, hwilon\n\u00dea gyt on orde stod Eadweard se langa, gearo and geornful, gylpwordum spr\u00e6c \u00fe\u00e6t he nolde fleogan\nHe br\u00e6c \u00feone bordweall and wi\u00f0 \u00fea beornas feaht, o\u00f0\u00fe\u00e6t he his sincgyfan on \u00feam s\u00e6mannum\nSwa dyde \u00c6\u00feeric, \u00e6\u00feele gefera, fus and for\u00f0georn, feaht eornoste.\nSibyrhtes bro\u00f0or and swi\u00f0e m\u00e6nig o\u00feer clufon cellod bord, cene hi weredon; b\u00e6rst bordes l\u00e6rig, and\n\u00dea \u00e6t gu\u00f0e sloh Offa \u00feone s\u00e6lidan, \u00fe\u00e6t he on eor\u00f0an feoll, and \u00f0\u00e6r Gaddes m\u00e6g grund gesohte.\nRa\u00f0e wear\u00f0 \u00e6t hilde Offa forheawen; he h\u00e6fde \u00f0eah gefor\u00feod \u00fe\u00e6t he his frean gehet, swa he beotode\n\u00d0a wear\u00f0 borda gebr\u00e6c.\nBrimmen wodon, gu\u00f0e gegremode; gar oft \u00feurhwod f\u00e6ges feorhhus.\nFor\u00f0 \u00fea eode Wistan, \u00feurstanes sunu, wi\u00f0 \u00feas secgas feaht; he w\u00e6s on ge\u00ferange hyra \u00fereora bana, \u00e6r\n\u00de\u00e6r w\u00e6s sti\u00f0 gemot; stodon f\u00e6ste wigan on gewinne, wigend cruncon, wundum werige.\nW\u00e6l feol on eor\u00fean.\nOswold and Eadwold ealle hwile, begen \u00fea gebro\u00feru, beornas trymedon, hyra winemagas wordon\nByrhtwold ma\u00feelode bord hafenode se w\u00e6s eald geneat, \u00e6sc acwehte; he ful baldlice beornas l\u00e6rde:\nHer li\u00f0 ure ealdor eall forheawen, god on greote.\nA m\u00e6g gnornian se \u00f0e nu fram \u00feis wigplegan wendan \u00feence\u00f0.\nIc eom frod feores; fram ic ne wille, ac ic me be healfe minum hlaforde, be swa leofan men, licgan\nSwa hi \u00c6\u00feelgares bearn ealle bylde, Godric to gu\u00fee.\nOft he gar forlet, w\u00e6lspere windan on \u00fea wicingas, swa he on \u00feam folce fyrmest eode, heow and\nN\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t na se Godric \u00fee \u00f0a gu\u00f0e forbeah",
